# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TEMPORARY. DELETE THIS FILE THE DAY `bizapps-accounting` IS PUBLISHED TO NPM.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# WHY IT IS HERE. `bizapps-accounting` is a MANDATORY peer dependency of this app — orders cannot
# book an order or a payment without it (see docs/dependency-on-accounting.md). The manifests now say
# so, correctly, with no `optional: true` escape hatch.
#
# But accounting is not published yet. npm 7+ installs peer dependencies automatically, so a
# mandatory peer it cannot fetch from the registry fails the whole install with E404 — verified:
#
#     npm error 404 '@mj-biz-apps/accounting-core-entities-server@>=0.1.0' is not in this registry.
#
# `legacy-peer-deps` tells npm not to auto-install peers. The dependency is still DECLARED and still
# mandatory; npm simply stops trying to fetch it, and `scripts/link-local-apps.mjs` symlinks the
# sibling checkout on postinstall as it always has.
#
# WHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not permission to run without accounting. The code statically imports
# `AccountingEngineBase` and calls it on every allocation; a genuinely absent package fails at module
# load. This only stops npm from trying to download something that does not exist yet.
#
# ON PUBLISH DAY: delete this file, run `npm install`, confirm the peers resolve from the registry,
# and remove the interim note from docs/dependency-on-accounting.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
legacy-peer-deps=true
